Acknowledge Bird Sound Recordists of BirdCLEF 2026 (Brazil's Pantanal)
Time to Acknowledge Bird Sound Recordists
On the previous competiton BirdCLEF 2023 (3 years ago) I wrote a topic:

Bird Sound Recordists. Competitions without them? I don't think so

Therefore I decided to acknowledge the Bird Sound Recordists of this BirdCLEF 2026 (Brazil's Pantanal).

On the Dataset, they can be found on the "author" column of the train csv file.

Some Lines about Jayrson Araujo de Oliveira (the longest bar on the barplot) :
"Professor passionate for Biology, especially Birds. He said that he is just beginning to learn about ornithology and intend to advance in my knowledge to the limit, especially recognition of songs' bird. The vast majority of the songs I put on this site are also on wikiaves.com.br."

https://xeno-canto.org/contributor/LXKLWEDKEM?pg=376&dir=0&order=tax&view=1

"University professor and ornithologist Jayrson Araújo was responsible for the first photographic record of the Yellow-headed Rail (Laterallus flavivente) in the state of Goiás, at the Lagoa Vargem Bonita Park in Goiânia. In the Central-West region, the animal had only been photographed once before, in Brasília, in the Federal District."

https://www.jornalopcao.com.br/ultimas-noticias/professor-e-pesquisador-da-ufg-faz-primeiro-registro-fotografica-da-sana-amarela-em-goias-636407/

It's also very nice to read that there are several women on the author's column


Many thanks for these Bird Sound Recordists. Without them, we won't have such data or any competition.

